# Neo Learn Vector parameters (docs/specs/neo-learn.md, neo-learn-controls.md A1 and A2.8). The order is permanent: songs and
# presets store values by position. The 12 controls are the six core ones, then the six global ones (Attack, Decay, Sustain, Release,
# Unison / Spread, Output). Each has a snake_case id, and the Explain text (How, Sound; the description is the How line).
# Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoLearnVector
namespace NeoBuzz.LearnVector
class NeoLearnVectorMachine
tracks 16
summary Teaching vector synth: one Dye Essence patch driven by 12 controls. Four sound sources sit at the corners of a diamond (west, east, north, south), a cursor mixes them, four palettes change the sources, and an orbit generator (circle, figure-8, diamond step, random drift) moves the cursor on its own, with an ADSR, unison and an output gain. Every control says what it does and what you will hear. Use it for evolving pads and textures, or to learn how crossfading four oscillators makes a timbre move.

group Core
VectorX          "Vector X (W-E)" 0 1000 500 bip
    id vector_x
    how Crossfades horizontally between the West oscillator source (-100%) and the East oscillator source (+100%).
    sound Sweeps the horizontal timbral balance between warm analog waveforms (West) and glassy digital/FM tones (East).

VectorY          "Vector Y (S-N)" 0 1000 500 bip
    id vector_y
    how Crossfades vertically between the South oscillator source (-100%) and the North oscillator source (+100%).
    sound Sweeps the vertical timbral balance between deep sub/pad foundations (South) and airy choir/noise textures (North).

CornerPalette    "Corner Palette" 0 3 0 enum Poly_Classic Cinema_Horizon Cyber_Pulse Organic_Hybrid
    id corner_palette
    how Loads curated 4-oscillator combinations into the N/S/E/W corners (`Poly Classic`, `Cinema Horizon`, `Cyber Pulse`, `Organic Hybrid`).
    sound Changes the four underlying sound sources being blended by the X-Y pad.

OrbitSpeed       "Orbit Rate" 0 1000 400 freq 0.05 12
    id orbit_speed
    how Controls the speed of the vector trajectory generator that automatically moves the cursor around `(vector_x, vector_y)`.
    sound Determines how slowly or rhythmically the 4 sound sources morph into one another.

OrbitRadius      "Orbit Depth" 0 1000 250 pct
    id orbit_radius
    how Sets the radius of the automated 2D movement around the manual X-Y center point.
    sound At 0% the mix stays fixed where you place the cursor; at 100% it sweeps all four corners continuously.

OrbitShape       "Orbit Path" 0 3 0 enum Circle Figure_8 Diamond_Step Random_Drift
    id orbit_shape
    how Selects the geometric trajectory of the automated vector motion (`Circle`, `Figure-8`, `Diamond Step`, `Random Drift`).
    sound Changes the rhythmic pattern and symmetry of the evolving timbral crossfades.

group Global
EnvAttack        "Attack" 0 1000 551 time 0.0005 5
    id env_attack
    how Sets the time required for the note's amplitude (and routed envelope modulation) to ramp from silence to full peak after a note-on trigger.
    sound Low values create immediate, percussive plucks; high values produce slow, swelling pads.
EnvDecay         "Decay" 0 1000 600 time 0.005 8
    id env_decay
    how Controls how long it takes for the signal to drop from peak level down to the sustain level while a key remains held.
    sound Short decay makes notes snappy and tight; longer decay gives a gradual piano- or bell-like fade.
EnvSustain       "Sustain" 0 1000 800 pct
    id env_sustain
    how Defines the steady-state volume level maintained for as long as a note is held after the Attack and Decay stages complete.
    sound At 0% the synth behaves like a plucked or struck instrument; at 100% it holds full organ-like volume.
EnvRelease       "Release" 0 1000 600 time 0.005 10
    id env_release
    how Sets the time required for the sound to fade from its current level to complete silence after the note is released.
    sound Short release stops notes abruptly; long release leaves an ambient tail that blends chords together.
UnisonDetune     "Unison / Spread" 0 1000 0 pct
    id unison_detune
    how 0% plays one voice per note; above 0% each note plays 5 detuned, stereo-spread voices (3 in Additive, Granular and Spectral), with detune (up to ±50 cents) and width growing with the value.
    sound Thickens thin waveforms into wide, chorus-like stereo leads and pads.
OutputGain       "Output" 0 1000 621 db -36 12
    id output_gain
    how Sets the level after synthesis. There is no limiter (NeoBuzz mixes in floating point); a clip light shows when the output passes 0 dBFS.
    sound Controls overall loudness; keep the clip light dark when the next machine expects levels at or below 0 dBFS.

# What the machine measures (NeoLearnVectorMachine.Readings, machine_readings): the output after Output, in dBFS.
reading rms_db dB | The output's RMS over about half a second (-inf: silence)
reading peak_db dB | The output's peak, falling 20 dB a second (-inf: silence)
reading active_voices notes | Notes sounding now (unison voices belong to their note)
